A||N||2||janak||Exhaust Manifold woes....HELP ME!!!||||8||
Z||000000||janak||03-27-2000||11:27 AM||||Ok, I was out with the Fiero, trying the change the O2 sensor, and the mount for the damn sensor twisted right off the manifold!! I guess I dont know my own strength, being able to strip cast iron, lol  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/rolleyes.gif">. But seriously, what options do I have, I am headed to the local Pick-A-Part to pull another manifold. What problems with a change over should I be watching out for? I cant believe this happened my first repair on the car!!!!!<P>Any help is greatly appreciated.<BR>Joe||||reg||8
Z||000001||Raydar||03-27-2000||12:01 PM||||Joe, <BR>Use plenty of Liquid Wrench. Let it marinate for a few hours. Then do it again. (This is assuming that you can let the car sit for a while.) <BR>Some folks would call this overkill, but it can't hurt. I've only ever had to cut one bolt, and that was because the head was partially rusted away, and the wrench wouldn't grip it. ||||reg||1
Z||000002||Gokart||03-27-2000||10:25 PM||||Did the same exact thing back in 95 when I had a coupe. I didn't know any better so I tried high temp JB weld to get the mount back on! <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/redface.gif"> It lasted a whole 5 minutes before I ended up giving the Fiero Store a call! If you can get the manifold off, maybe you could have it welded back on? Not with JB weld though! <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/rolleyes.gif">||||reg||11
